 "job": {
  "owner": "Claude LEAD2-HBM/L2H-SM9",
  "branch": "claude/l2h-sm9-1019",
  "tag": "rp4hn_b_km64cx",
  "purpose": "HBM SM tile rp4, safe-design successor of smh_tile_rp4lp as two hardened halves (this kit = the n half, soft beat transits, 864 um (frame row unchanged with s_b); x store at x 86.4 (W channel 84 um)); closure of the MATVEC tile body (template of the rp4a attention tile).",
  "structural_change": "smh_tile_rp4lp (457.92 x 1598.4, aspect 3.49, 13/18 macros off the 43.2 lattice, 2,069-b landing read select 8,284 loads, gate1 GRT ovf 51,363, gate2 CTS rc 2) split along its lp region cut into two hardened halves (ot_hbm_smh_rp4h_n / _s) abutting in the SM frame slot: no landing (registered tile-to-tile crossing on the abutment face, judged per linked child-flop pair at die level), the two hard 216x43.2 land children replaced by soft kept landing registers (rl1 no longer crosses a macro), every macro on the 43.2 lattice, BF16 columns / transpose re-oriented so operand inputs face the x store and sums face the transpose, one clock root per half with clk on the abutment face beside the s half's.  Latency identical to the lp record (gout +3, all else 0).  SAFE2 successor of smh_rp4hn_b1019 (its gate failed the clock rule: one spine root from the abutment corner, TT insertion ~2.1 ns, boundary pin-flop spread ~200 ps): regional k-means clock roots (clock_split_km.tcl K=64, each root <= ~115 um across) under one balanced CTS top tree, hard-child clock pins on TritonCTS macro trees (lib insertion), clk entry moved to the W face at the half's centre height; io_hold_margin 0.03; x store moved to x 86.4 (W channel 41 -> 84 um: n_b GRT ovf 12,845 at the xs W channel / E end from its 3-face o_ix pins).  Cycles unchanged.",
  "extra_paths": [
   "tools/hbm_sm_repack_1015",
   "rtl/hbm_accel/sm/repack/h2",
   "results/arch/l2h_sm9_1019/bench"
  ],
  "benches": [
   {
    "name": "h2_lockstepsb",
    "cmd": "bash rtl/hbm_accel/sm/repack/h2/run_rp4h2_one.sh {RUN}/h2sb 0 1",
    "expect": "pass",
    "pass_regex": "^H2_LOCKSTEP PASS MUT=0 compared=",
    "pass_witness": "results/arch/l2h_sm9_1019/bench/mutsb0.log",
    "threads": 4,
    "peak_ram_gb": 48
   },
   {
    "name": "h2_mutsb1",
    "cmd": "bash rtl/hbm_accel/sm/repack/h2/run_rp4h2_one.sh {RUN}/h2msb1 1 1",
    "expect": "fail",
    "fail_regex": "^H2_LOCKSTEP FAIL MUT=1 mismatches=[1-9]",
    "fail_witness": "results/arch/l2h_sm9_1019/bench/mutsb1.log",
    "threads": 4,
    "peak_ram_gb": 48
   },
   {
    "name": "h2_mut2",
    "cmd": "bash rtl/hbm_accel/sm/repack/h2/run_rp4h2_one.sh {RUN}/h2m2 2 0",
    "expect": "fail",
    "fail_regex": "^H2_LOCKSTEP FAIL MUT=2 mismatches=[1-9]",
    "fail_witness": "results/arch/l2h_sm9_1019/bench/mut2.log",
    "threads": 4,
    "peak_ram_gb": 48
   },
   {
    "name": "h2_mut3",
